.TH GGE\-INPUT 7 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
gge\-input \- keys, mouse, gamepad, actions, text input
.SH DESCRIPTION
Input is polled once per frame into
.B Engine.input
and passed to the top scene's
.B handle_input
as
.BR "const Input *in" .
Only the top scene receives it.
.SS Raw queries
.BR key_down (3)
(held),
.BR key_pressed (3)
(this frame),
.BR key_released (3);
the same three for
.BR mouse_* (3)
with
.B MOUSE_LEFT/RIGHT/MIDDLE
and for
.BR pad_* (3)
with
.BR PAD_* .
Key names are
.BR KEY_A ", " KEY_ESCAPE ", " KEY_ENTER ", " KEY_BACKSPACE ", " KEY_SPACE ...
from keys.h. Mouse position is
.BR in->mouse_x ", " in->mouse_y
in logical pixels.
.SS Actions
Bind named actions to keys, pad buttons and axes so scenes never hard\-code
keys:
.nf
.ft B
enum { LEFT, RIGHT, JUMP };
static ActionMap keys;
action_map_init(&keys);
action_bind_key(&keys, JUMP, KEY_SPACE);
action_bind_pad(&keys, JUMP, PAD_SOUTH);
if (action_pressed(&keys, in, JUMP)) ...
float x = action_axis(&keys, in, LEFT, RIGHT);   /* -1..1 */
.ft R
.fi
.SS Text input
.BR engine_text_input (3)
turns on delivery of typed characters into
.B in->text
(a short string per frame). Turn it on in
.B on_enter
and off in
.BR on_exit .
Letter keys still register as key presses while it is on.
.SS Where to read input
Only in
.BR handle_input
(display rate) for one\-shot reactions, or via
.B &e->input
inside
.B update
(tick rate) for movement. Never move things from handle_input.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR key_pressed (3),
.BR action_bind_key (3),
.BR action_axis (3),
.BR engine_text_input (3),
.BR gge\-scenes (7)
